CORE gcc-only
main.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ store then load: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ fetch_add: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Clang's __c11_atomic_load/store/fetch_add intrinsics (what <stdatomic.h>
expands to under Clang) are polymorphic in the atomic object's type, like
GCC's __atomic_load_n & co.; they are typed and implemented as those.
Previously a varargs declaration returning void took precedence and the
result could not be used ("conversion from 'void' to 'signed int'").
